.TH MYSTRNCPY 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
mystrncpy \- copy a bounded number of characters from a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "int mystrncpy(char *" dest ", const char *" src ", int " n );
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mystrncpy()
function copies at most
.I n
characters from the string pointed to by
.I src
into the buffer pointed to by
.I dest,
and always null-terminates the result.
If
.I src
is shorter than
.I n,
copying stops early at the source string's null terminator.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success.
